2026-11-13T04:15:16.8707732Z #!/usr/bin/env python3
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8708274Z """Bounded audit-readiness dossier for a resumed product snapshot.
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8708753Z 
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8708894Z Why this exists
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8709247Z ---------------
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8709873Z Run 40196023042's producer finished cleanly and persisted a real delta, but its
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8710810Z independent audit died at ``LEX_WORK_QUANTUM_EXPIRED seconds=2700`` (exit 78)
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8711689Z before writing a gate.  The next auditor should not have to spend its own
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8712886Z quantum rediscovering the slice, the accepted pointer or which artifacts are
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8713820Z claim-bearing.  This module gives it one command that re-derives the snapshot's
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8714307Z claims on bounded inputs and records the exact evidence.
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8714555Z 
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8714633Z What it does
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8714825Z ------------
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8715054Z * runs the product-owned state contract;
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8715410Z * checks the fail-closed posture and the accepted pointer;
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8715858Z * re-classifies the resumed run from its committed run/jobs snapshot;
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8716328Z * verifies the resumed run's committed diagnosis (quantum expiry, durable
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8716714Z   delta, unadjudicated status);
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8717362Z * hashes and structurally checks the claim-bearing artifacts (including the
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8717811Z   before/after bytes for the v68 rejection/incumbent leg);
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8718255Z * re-runs the shipped progressive query smoke over a real socket in fixture
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8718653Z   mode (no network, no paid inference);
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8718947Z * runs the bounded MVP core pytest set;
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8719350Z * confirms the producer wrote no auditor-namespace path and minted no gate.
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8770037Z 
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8770334Z It deliberately does NOT write ``results/audit/**``, mint a gate, score a
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8770876Z frozen bar, re-run a serve verdict, or label any run accepted/rejected.  Its
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8771513Z output is a dossier for the independent auditor, never a verdict.
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8771982Z 
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8772116Z Usage
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8772437Z -----
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8772904Z     python3 product/audit_readiness.py --run-id 40200882831 \\
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8773559Z         --out results/product/audit_readiness/CYCLE_40200882831_audit_readiness.json
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8773901Z 
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8774066Z     # fast mode while iterating (skip the two slow re-runs):
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8774573Z     python3 product/audit_readiness.py --run-id X --skip-tests --skip-smoke --out /tmp/x.json
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8775091Z """
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8775413Z from __future__ import annotations
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8775693Z 
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8775832Z import argparse
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8776135Z import hashlib
2026-11-13T04:15:16.8776444Z import json
