2026-11-13T04:26:30.1655659Z Why this exists
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1655852Z ---------------
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1656177Z The audit of rejected product cycle 39139648336 (round 3, repaired in round 4)
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1656801Z returned exactly one required fix: ``reports/product/CYCLE_39139648336.md`` §3 F1
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1657602Z described the live sourced answer as "(6 cited, live free model)" while the
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1658128Z artifact of record ``results/product/live_slice/CYCLE_39139648336_F1F2_VERIFY.json``
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1658662Z records ``answer.n_cited=5``, and the answer prose cites exactly those 5 retrieved
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1659102Z decisions. The report overstated the answer by one.
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1659333Z 
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1659542Z That is the same defect class as the 13 -> 17 test-count error this repair chain
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1660035Z corrected (audit F4), as RF2's "+7 tests" against a measured +10, and as RF-1's
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1660545Z false attribution of a +21 collected-test delta to the cycle that did not produce
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1661063Z it. Every occurrence was a number typed into prose instead of derived from the
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1661563Z measurement it summarises. The lane's rule for correcting such a number is RF2
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1662082Z arithmetic discipline - publish BOTH numbers, side by side, so the correction is
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1662492Z auditable rather than silent.
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1662654Z 
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1662831Z WHAT THIS GUARD DOES AND DOES NOT COVER (measured, not aspirational)
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1663241Z ---------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1663851Z Audit RF-2 of the round-4 cycle found the round-4 guard shipped with a claim that
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1664358Z overstated it ("the two ways the sweep could be weakened"), and measured three
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1664847Z escape paths it could not see. This module's scope is therefore stated as a
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1665354Z MEASUREMENT and pinned by ``test_measured_scope_is_published_not_aspirational``:
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1665661Z 
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1665885Z * covered: citation-count claims, in BOTH directions of phrasing, in every report
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1666378Z   that cites a live-slice artifact by filename (measured: 2 artifacts, 3
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1666804Z   artifact/report pairs, 13 parsed citation claims);
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1667350Z * covered since round 5: the inverted phrasing "cited N decisions", correction
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1667848Z   markers that must be word-boundary and same-sentence, and the internal
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1668342Z   arithmetic of any test-count decomposition ("+21 = +11 + +2 + +4 + +4") in any
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1668760Z   report, which needs no artifact to check;
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1669156Z * covered by a separate module (the attribution is a MEASUREMENT, not a prose
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1669634Z   claim): which commit produced each part of a collected-test delta -
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1670341Z   ``product/test_delta_attribution.py`` + ``product/tests/test_delta_attribution.py``;
2026-11-13T04:26:30.1670846Z * covered since the round-1 repair of rejected cycle 39891382087: the
